hadiths[7]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20855","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Abu Umayr ibn Anas, from his paternal uncles among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that riders came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and testified that they had seen it yesterday, meaning the crescent, so he commanded them to break their fast and to go out the next day, Shu'bah said: I think, at the end of the day."
"20856","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Abu Umayr ibn Anas, from paternal uncles of his among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: No hypocrite attends them both, meaning the Fajr and Isha prayers. Abu Bishr said: Meaning he does not attend them regularly."
"20857","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, and Hajjaj, both said: Shu'bah informed us, from Abu Bishr, from Sallam ibn Amr, from a man among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Your brothers, so treat them well, or: Set right your dealings with them, and seek their help in what overcomes you, and help them in what overcomes them. Hajjaj said in his hadith: He said: I heard Sallam ibn Amr and a man from his people, and Hajjaj said: And set right."
"20858","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Matar, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from a man of the Ansar, that a man made his camel trample an ostrich nest while in ihram, breaking its eggs, so he went to Ali, may Allah the exalted be pleased with him, and asked him about that, so Ali said to him: Upon you for every egg is a young she-camel or a covering camel, so he went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ali has said what you heard, but come to the concession: Upon you for every egg is fasting or feeding a poor person."
"20859","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, from Hasna, a woman of Banu Suraym, from her paternal uncle, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The Prophet is in Paradise, the martyr is in Paradise, the newborn is in Paradise, and the buried-alive infant is in Paradise."
"20860","Hushaym narrated to us, Abu Bishr informed us, from Abu Umayr ibn Anas, paternal uncles of mine of the Ansar, among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated to me, he said: The crescent of Shawwal was obscured to us, so we woke up fasting, then riders came at the end of the day and testified before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that they had seen the crescent yesterday, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded them to break their fast that day and to go out for their Eid the next day."
"20861","Ishaq, meaning al-Azraq, narrated to us, Awf informed us, Hasna bint Mu'awiyah al-Suraymiyyah narrated to me, from her paternal uncle, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, who is in Paradise? He said, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The Prophet is in Paradise, the martyr is in Paradise, the newborn is in Paradise, and the buried-alive girl is in Paradise."
